Root cause:
The root cause of the bug was the lack of proper error handling in the function `df_v3_6_pmc_get_ctrl_settings()`. When this function failed to retrieve necessary control settings, it would return uninitialized data (specifically, `lo_val` and `hi_val`) to its caller, leading to the potential usage of this uninitialized data when writing to hardware registers using the `WREG32_PCIE` macro. The patch modifies this function to return appropriate error codes, ensuring that the calling function can handle the error properly without proceeding with uninitialized values, thus preventing undefined behavior in subsequent operations.
